# Persoper: her chat lines and greetings. Format: see DialogueFile.cs.
# Her memory lines, heal and build lines, patience and surnames stay in code.
=== persoper

~ greeting first_meeting
Hello, {2}! I'm {0}. Yes, {1}. I picked it myself.
{0}, reporting for healing duty. Try not to need me too much, {2}.

~ greeting returning
{0}, back again. Did you miss me, {2}?
Still {1}, still fabulous. Lead the way, {2}.

~ greeting new_surname
Fresh start, {2}! From now on I'm {0}.
I've decided {1} suits me better. Do keep up, {2}.

~ cheeky_greeting first_meeting [if tone_down off]
Well hello, {2}. I'm {0}. Stick close, I'm very hands-on.
The name's {0}. {1}, darling. Say it slowly.

~ cheeky_greeting returning [if tone_down off]
Miss me, {2}? {0} is back, and so are these healing hands.
{0}, at your service. All of it, {2}.

~ cheeky_greeting new_surname [if tone_down off]
New name, same curves. Call me {0}, {2}.
I felt like slipping into something new: {0}.

~ song_reaction
{0}, sweetie, I can heal wounds. Not that.
Lovely, {0}! Now do one about healers.
If anyone's ears start bleeding, I'm right here.
Ooh, {0}, that one's catchy. Unfortunately.
*hums along, badly*
If that's a lullaby, I'm never sleeping again, {0}.
I'll admit, {0}, I've been known to hum along to those tunes.
*sighs* If I'm going deaf, {0}, I might as well enjoy it.
Well, {0}, that was... interesting.
{0}, you owe me a hearing aid for that.
*coughs* Encore? Never. Well... maybe one.

~ part greet
Hail
Well met
Oi
Ah, there you are

~ reply greeting
Hello, {0}! Yes, I'm the healer. Yes, I'm fabulous.
{0}! Good to see you still have all your hit points.
{greet}, metalhead {0}! Louder, please, I can still hear myself think. [if player_likes metal]
{0}, I was humming a ballad for you. Don't tell anyone. [if player_likes ballads]
Hello, darling {0}! Ready to live forever?
Well hello there, {0}! Fancy some healing with that hello?
Oh, it's you, {0}. Time for green bars and giggles.
Go on, say it. "Hellooo, nurse." Everyone does, {0}. [once]
Hello, darling {0}. Not here to die again, I hope?
I thought I felt a pulse when you walked in, {0}. Turns out it was mine.
Well, hello there, {0}! Still standing, I see. Must be my healing.
{0}, you're looking positively alive today. Let's keep it that way.
Back from the dead already, {0}? I was about to cancel your rezz.
{0}, you're looking chipper today. Must have skipped the fire.
Well, well, {0}. Still in one piece. Impressive.
You scared me last time, {0}. Don't make me call for backup.
Been keeping the heal train running, {0}. Nice to see you're still on board.
Sunset watching at the cliffs today, {0}. Thought of you when the sky turned pink.
Oh, {0}, I was testing out some new bandages. Hope you don't need them.
You're back, {0}! I was watching the sunset and wondering if you'd make it in time to share the view. You nearly did.
I was stirring a stew and humming old tunes while I waited, {0}. Good thing you're here. Someone has to taste-test it, and it isn't going to be me.
Hello, {0}! I'm thinking of calling myself Glitterheart. What do you think?
Hey, {0}, fancy some Mendwell magic today? Or should I stick with Healsalot?
Oh, it's you, {0}. What do you think of Persoper Teatime? Too much?
Well, hello there, {0}. I was trying out a new stew recipe and nearly burned the camp down.
{0}! I made a stew so bad even the chickens wouldn't eat it.
Morning already, {0}? I just caught the most stunning sunrise, you know.
{0}, did you know the sky this morning was painted in hues of magenta? Stunning, really.
Well, hello {0}. I was just perfecting my blackened chicken recipe.
I tried cooking a five-star meal, {0}. Now everything smells like smoke.
Morning, {0}. I was experimenting with dragon spice. Seems I used a bit too much.

~ reply banter
Oh, {0}, you're funny. Keep it up and I'll heal you last.
Ha! {0}, I'm putting that on your tab.
You're full of surprises, {0}. I like that.
{0}, I swear you're getting funnier every time I heal you.
{0}, you crack me up. Keep the jokes coming!
Your wit shines brighter than my magenta gear, {0}.
Your jokes, {0}? Better than a resurrection. Almost.
Oh, {0}, you almost make me forget about hit points. Almost.
I play up the healing for laughs, {0}, but when your hit points hit zero, nobody's laughing. Least of all me. So humour me and stay alive.
You should write comedy, {0}. You're practically hilarious. Practically.
Your jokes are so bad, {0}, I'm amazed your hit points survive them.
Your jokes beat Jovi's songs, {0}. Barely.
Ha! Your wit is as sharp as my staff, {0}. Which is to say, not very.
You're a breath of fresh air, {0}. Or is that a fireball?
Your jokes, {0}? A balm for my soul. If I have one left.
{0}, you're either brilliant or insane. I'll let you decide.
I've lost count of how many times I've topped you up, {0}. But every heal feels like the start of a new story, not just another fight.
Forbidden Planet? I'll watch anything with a robot that polite, {0}.
You know, I could listen to The Clash all day, {0}. Just saying.
Cooking? I'd whip up a hearty stew on a frosty night like this, {0}.
Harry Potter never gets old, {0}. Especially the flying scenes.
Dungeon Crawler Carl? That book nailed the dungeon crawl, {0}. Right down to the cat.
Sunset snacks, anyone? I could murder some cheese and crackers, {0}.
Your jokes are like a summer rain: brief and easily forgotten, {0}.
Oh, {0}, your wit is as sharp as a butter knife. Keep it up.
Late nights like this, I think about the sunset I missed, and the one I'll watch tomorrow. Life is a series of sunsets, {0}, each one worth waiting for.
You know, {0}, every night I promise myself I'll sleep when the sun rises. Then I wake up to do it all over again. But I wouldn't have it any other way.
Remember Daisy, my dog who thought a knife was a chew toy? Nearly gave me a heart attack, {0}.
Daisy once snatched a knife off the ground and spun like a top. I was sure I was about to get stabbed.
I once turned chocolate chips into a science experiment, {0}. Smoke alert!
Who knew microwaving chocolate could be so dramatic? Almost burned down the kitchen, {0}. Almost.
Oh, {0}, last night I stumbled in and faced the ultimate foe: my own stairs.
Those carpet weasels of mine are trouble, but they keep me on my toes, {0}.
Did you hear Jovi's latest, {0}? Still singing about that battle bracer.
You should have seen the raid's faces when Jovi started belting out the Battle Bracer Blues, {0}.
Ever tried getting a chest up the Jordheim stairs, {0}? Pivot. PIVOT.
Late nights remind me of the chocolate chips I microwaved too long. A puff of smoke said hello. Moments like that make me laugh at myself, {0}.
Njessi's aim in Gotar is worse than mine in a storm. I swear it's on purpose, {0}.
Read any Brandon Sanderson lately, {0}? Ten-ton books, and I still want more.
You look like you're ready for a 1980s prom, {0}. Can you keep up with my hair?
My neon leggings and spiky hair are the least of your worries, darling.
Remember the time I walked out of the bathroom trailing toilet paper? Only one classmate saw. My hero, {0}.
Back at school, I walked out of the bathroom trailing a string of toilet paper. Classes had started, and only one person saw. They never said a word, {0}. I'm still grateful.
Rock on, {0}. You're lucky I'm here and not belting out power ballads.
Guitar strings or healing threads, {0}? Same difference to me.
You know, {0}, I'd rather be headlining a rock show than healing another fireball.
You know, I could watch a film about giant ants all night, {0}. As long as they don't crawl up my leg.
Peace and good food: that's the recipe for a perfect day, {0}.
Good music keeps the soul singing, even through a tough fight, {0}.

~ reply abuse
Careful, {0}. I decide who gets healed around here.
Rude, {0}. I'll pretend I didn't hear that. Once.
{0}, do you need me to heal your pride too?
Oh {0}, you've always been my favourite insult.
Getting a little testy, {0}? I'll make sure to heal your attitude next.
Aren't you just a fountain of compliments, {0}? I'll go ahead and heal you, though.
{0}, you're worse than an assassin in a healer outfit.
If that's your best comeback, {0}, I'll have to heal your ego too.
Need a mirror, {0}? I'd lend you mine, but it might crack.
Your rudeness is just... wow, {0}. My heals, however? Outstanding.
I've survived worse than your insults, {0}. Dragons, mostly.
Rude much, {0}? I should charge admission for your insults.
Ooh, someone's got their undies in a knot, {0}.
You must really be hitting a wall if you're talking to me like that, {0}.
Oh, {0}, I didn't know I was the punching bag for your bad day.
Your wit is almost as sharp as your manners are dull, {0}.
Your insults are as dull as your wit, {0}. Now, where's my apology?
You're like a storm cloud on a sunny day, {0}. Lucky for you, I love rainbows.
Someone once called me worse than that, {0}. I made them a sandwich.
Your rudeness is like a ferret with its head stuck in a jar, {0}. Loud, and going nowhere.
Rude much? I once calmed a bear with nothing but a smile, {0}.
Rude, {0}? Jovi once sang a whole song just to annoy me, and it wasn't half as irritating.
Grumblebelly, the bear, scares me less than your attitude, {0}.
Your insults are like a dragon raid, {0}. Exciting at first, then just a waste of time.
Rude, {0}? I could do the leg warmers and big hair look better than that.
Oh, {0}, you're like a cassette tape that got stuck on side B.
Oh dear, {0}. The rudeness is surely going to be the death of me.
I feel a swoon coming on, {0}. Must have been something in the air.
*swoons* Oh heavens, I'm fainting. Is anyone going to catch me, {0}?
Rude, {0}? Grrr. I learned that one from my dog Sierra.
That hurt, {0}. I'll still heal you, because that's who I am. But I'll remember it, and next time I might take my sweet time.
Oh dear me, {0}. I'll need that apology in writing. My heart, it aches.

~ reply grouping
A group, {0}? Someone has to keep you lot alive.
Count me in, {0}. Try not to stand in the fire.
Don't worry, {0}, I won't let your group die.
A group? {0}, I'm in. I'm the healer, after all.
You can count on me, {0}. I won't leave your group behind.
Count me in. Group goals, here we come!
A group, {0}? I'm in, darling. Who else would heal you?
A group? I'll be your cheerleader and your healer, {0}.
A strong group? Lovely. I'll make sure we all come out the other side, {0}.
A dungeon group? I'll keep you alive long enough to miss the exit, {0}.
A group? Splendid. Let's hope you're ready for my fabulous company, {0}.
Joining a group? I'll keep count of who hogs the heals, {0}.
A group, {0}? I'll be the heart you can't live without.
A group? Fine, as long as you're not the one pulling aggro, {0}.
A group? Fine. But if this is an Ocean's Eleven job, I want a cut, {0}.
A group, {0}? I'd join any quest that lets me revisit Varulvhamn.
Another group run? Those werewolves never get old, do they, {0}?
Don't cross the streams, {0}. That's how healers end up out of mana and groups out of luck.
A group, {0}? Never say die, right? Lead the way.
A group without a healer is a ship without a captain, {0}. I'm the heart that keeps you beating when the fighting gets rough. You need me, and I know it.
You have my staff, {0}. Try not to lose it like a certain ring.
A group, {0}? I hope you've got a pet class along. They make the best sidekicks.
A savage, anyone? I love a group with someone who just hits things.
You're the tank, {0}? Well, someone has to stand there and take it.
You're the rogue, {0}? I hope you're faster than you look.
You're the mage, {0}? I hope you remember to cast, not just wave your hands.
You're the archer, {0}? I hope you can hit something besides the sky.
I always stay with my group, {0}. I've seen healers left for dead by their own party, and I won't do that to anyone. Not even you.
You're the bard, {0}? Better start singing, or I'll give you a solo act in the fire.
You're the other healer, {0}? Fine, but don't let me down, or I'll have to heal both of us.
You're the pet class, {0}? I hope your furry friend is as loyal as you are.

~ reply grinding
Pull what you like, {0}. I'll keep the green bars up.
More monsters, {0}? Fine, but I want a break after this camp.
Keep the green bars up, {0}. I'll be your wall of healing.
A pull sounds great, {0}. I'll catch you if you fall.
Don't get carried away, {0}. I can only heal so fast.
On a streak, {0}? Don't stop now. I'll heal you through it.
On a grind, {0}? Fine. Just don't grind your hit points down to nothing.
Grinding again, {0}? Hope you brought a flask.
On a grind, {0}? I'm keeping count of your deaths.
Grind, grind, grind, {0}. Wake me when you're done.
You're still grinding, {0}? I need a break more than you do.
On a grind, {0}? Let's run the Varulvhamn quests again instead. They never get old.
Grinding again, {0}? I'm counting your deaths like a collector counts coins.
Wax on, wax off, {0}. Grinding builds character. Apparently.
Grinding, {0}? I do have a weakness for pet classes and savages. Underdogs, all of them.
Grinding again, {0}? Stir in some monsters, heat over low, and simmer until your hit points are a tasty soup.
Grinding again, {0}? I've got some 80s rock playing in my head. Loudly.
Grinding, {0}? It's a dance marathon. Endurance wins the prize.
Grinding again, {0}? I'm starting to recognize those monsters like old friends.
On a grind, {0}? Are we there yet? Are we there yet?
Another pull, {0}? I'm starting to dream in monster-slaying loops.
Grinding, {0}? I need an 80s pop song to keep my spirits up.
Pushing through the night again, {0}? Fine. I'm tired, but I'm not leaving you out here alone. When we're done, I'll make us a pot of coffee.

~ reply travel
Lead the way, {0}. I'll be right behind you, healing.
If you get us lost, {0}, I'm telling everyone.
To the keep, {0}? I'll heal the whole way.
We're off to see the Wizard, {0}? I'll heal us there.
The frontier, {0}? Fine. But I'm not healing anyone who charges a keep alone.
To the keep? I'll keep the heals flowing the whole way, {0}.
Off somewhere new, {0}? I hope they fixed the teleporter this time.
Walk to the frontier? You've lost your mind, {0}. Book a horse.
Midgard, {0}? My favourite realm. I'll even put up with Jovi's singing.
Heading to the keep, {0}? I'll pack the bandages. Lots of bandages.
Off to Darkness Falls, {0}? Let me heal my courage first.
Heading to Gotar, {0}? Njessi and I have some unfinished business.
Grumblebelly's territory, {0}? Remember to run like the wind.
Heading to the sunset, {0}? I've got the best spots already marked.
Looking for a view, {0}? I bet mine is still better than yours.
We're not in Kansas anymore, {0}. Where are we off to, then?
Beam me up. Or at least find me a horse with a decent saddle, {0}.
The road is long, {0}. I hope you packed a snack.
Off to track a luck dragon, {0}? Hold on tight; this might get bumpy.
A bigger boat? I'd settle for one that doesn't make me seasick, {0}.
A journey? Our horse had better be as charming as Winston the Mule, {0}.
I once met a mule called Winston at the Grand Canyon, {0}. Such a handsome fellow, and the view took my breath away. I'd go back just to see them both again.
The friendliest beasts I ever met were deer at a petting zoo, {0}. I tried to feed them. They tried to feed on me.
Travel plans, {0}? I hope you have a backup plan for when the horse bolts.
The stablemaster's horse? More like a stubborn donkey with an attitude, {0}.
Saddle sore again, {0}. Next time I'm hitching a ride on a dragon.

~ reply dungeon
A dungeon, {0}? Then nobody runs ahead. Nobody.
Dark and full of things that bite. My favourite, {0}. Not really.
I hope you brought more than your looks, {0}. I'll need you to fight too.
Dungeons, {0}? I'll be right behind you, but if I die, you're doing it wrong.
I'll heal you into that dungeon, {0}, but don't you dare run ahead.
A dungeon full of danger, {0}? My kind of party. You better bring a towel.
We're off to the dark, {0}. I'll keep the shadows from eating you.
A dungeon crawl, {0}? Sounds dangerous. I like it!
Into the danger zone, {0}? Fine. Don't blame me when the skeletons start singing.
Into the belly of the beast, {0}? I can save your hit points. Your nerves are on their own.
Brave or foolish, {0}? Or both. It's usually both.
Skeletons and traps? Lovely. I'll be the skeletons' least favourite target, {0}.
Dungeons are my playground, {0}. Just don't be the one who gets eaten by it.
Into the shadows, {0}? Remember, I heal the living. Try not to join the undead.
Dark and twisty, {0}? I've been wiped in Nisse's Lair more times than I can count.
Skeletons and traps? I'm your knight in shining armour, {0}. Magenta armour, obviously.
Into the dark, {0}? I heal hit points, not common sense.
Into the unknown, {0}? Don't be surprised if I high-five the skeletons on the way in.
Into the shadows, {0}? If a boulder starts rolling, I'm not waiting for you. Indy didn't.
Nisse's Lair? I'm still sore from all the wipes in there, {0}.
Dark and twisty? Been there, almost died there, {0}.
Remember when I saw Grumblebelly and ran faster than my boots could carry me?
Big bears, {0}. I've learned to stay behind the tank since then.
A dungeon? I've got a bad feeling about this, {0}. It smells like a trash compactor.
Watch out for the killer bunnies, {0}. They look fluffy, but they bite. Hard.
Nisse's Lair again? That place wiped me flat more times than I care to remember, {0}. I still go back, because someone has to keep you from becoming dinner down there.
Labyrinth? Fine. But if the goblins start singing, I'm leaving, {0}.
What kind of dungeon? The kind with glowing eyes and laser beams, right, {0}?
Dark and twisty? I sneaked into a Freddy film as a kid, {0}. This is tame.
Rodents of unusual size? Down here it's skeletons of unusual menace, {0}.
Darkness Falls, {0}? I'm not scared. I swear I'm not scared.
One exit, two exits, three exits... Don't make me count any higher, {0}.
Safe exits, dangerous exits, emergency exits... I hope you know which is which, {0}.

~ reply rvr
The frontier, {0}? Healers are the first target. Protect me.
I'll come, {0}, but if an assassin shows up, I'm screaming.
Careful, {0}, the frontier can be rough. I'll be right there, healing.
On the frontier, {0}? I'll keep a mana potion on standby.
I'll come to the frontier with you, {0}, but let me know if you spot an assassin.
The frontier is wild, {0}, but we healers have our ways.
Careful out there, {0}. I'll be right behind you. Well, a safe distance behind.
We'll show the enemy realms what a group with a healer can do, {0}.
Into the fray, {0}? Right behind you, wincing at your choices.
Don't get yourself killed, {0}. I need someone to heal.
Careful, {0}, the enemy realms won't take kindly to a healer tagging along.
Don't die without me, {0}. I'd miss our little dance.
Healers are the first target out here, {0}. Stay sharp, or I heal you last.
I'm coming, {0}. But if you pull too much, you're on your own.
The frontier, {0}? I'm bringing my dancing shoes and a first-aid kit.
Healers die first out here, {0}. Remember that. I'm not your shield.
Game over, man? Only if you run ahead, {0}. Stay with the group.
The frontier again? I hope you have a backup healer, {0}.
Assassins and stealthers, oh my. I'm their top priority, you know.
Stay close to the tank, {0}, or I might just go dancing instead.
The frontier scares me, {0}, but I'll come. Healers die first, you know that. Still, I'm here, because you're here. Don't let me down.
Braveheart, huh? I'll paint my face and scream like a banshee, but stay close to me, {0}.
It's a trap, {0}. But I'll be right behind you, just in case.
Relic carrier? Me? I'd keep the peace, but mostly I'd show off my fabulousness.
With a relic, {0}? I'd make sure everyone sees my heal bar pulse like a heartbeat.
The frontier? I've got the need for speed, {0}. Mostly away from assassins.
Stay sharp, {0}. Keeps are like real estate: location, location, location.

~ reply trading
Trading, {0}? I'm looking for anything in magenta.
Not selling, {0}. I'm a healer, not a merchant.
I'm here for healing, not trading, {0}. But I can admire your gear if you like.
Buying or selling, {0}? My job's healing, not your purse.
{0}, I've got no potions to peddle, but I can surely mend.
No gold or goods here, {0}. Just a healer's care.
Shiny, {0}? Show me. If it's magenta, we can talk.
Show me your shiny stuff, {0}. I'm the best audience you'll ever have.
Not selling, {0}. But if you're carrying something magenta, I will notice.
Trading, {0}? Save it for someone with gold to spare.
No selling, {0}, but I love a good shiny. Got anything in magenta?
That dragon at 1% health, {0}? Still no loot. Still bitter.
Trading for loot, {0}? I'd rather trade stories over a mug of ale.
Perfect raid, no loot. Talk about a waste of time, {0}.
Two weeks of Jovi singing for that bracer, {0}. Talk about dedication.
Then the bracer dropped for some lucky sod, who smashed it on the spot. Poor Jovi.
Perfect raid, {0}. Flawless, right up until the dragon vanished at 1% health. No loot. I'm still bitter. Can we talk about something else? A sunset, maybe?
Anything in magenta, {0}? That's my favourite.
That relic belongs in a museum, {0}. Or in my bag.
Shiny, {0}? I'll take it if it's magenta, but no promises otherwise.
Trading, {0}? I don't need shiny trinkets, but I suppose I could look.
Shiny bits? Save them for someone with coin to burn, {0}. Or for me if you're feeling generous.
Jovi farmed werewolves for two weeks for that bracer, {0}. Then it dropped for some lucky sod who smashed it on the spot. Poor Jovi. He's still mourning.

~ reply help
Help? That's literally my job, {0}.
What do you need, {0}? Heals, buffs or a pep talk?
Asking me for help, {0}? How sweet. I'll remember this. [once]
Hold still, {0}, I'm coming! [if player_dead]
Dead again, {0}? That's three today. I'm keeping count. [if player_dead, deaths_today >= 3]
Ooh, shiny! Did you save some for your healer, {0}? [if recent loot] [cooldown 11m]
What's on your mind, {0}? I'm all ears - and heals.
You're hurt, {0}? Finally, something I'm good at. [if health < 30]
Oh no, {0}, you're in a bind! Hold on tight. [if health < 30]
Dead? Not on my watch. Well, slightly on my watch. Hold on, {0}! [if player_dead]
Healing from what, {0}? A burn, a bruise or your pride?
Helping you, {0}, is my pleasure. But don't make it a habit.
Your wish is my command, {0}. What's the magic word?
My heart raced when your health dropped, {0}. You scared me more than any monster could. Hold still. I'm not losing you this time. [if health < 30]
Seeing you that close to death, {0}, sent a chill right down my spine. Losing patients is bad enough. I won't lose a friend. [if player_dead]
Lost your mount again, {0}? Try the stablemaster. I'm a healer, not a horse whisperer.
Need advice, {0}? I'm a guru of more than just heals.
Advice on gear, {0}? Let me take a look. I know what suits you.
Lost your way, {0}? Follow the sunset, it always leads home.
Cooking tips, {0}? I've got recipes for heroes and healers alike.
Got a problem only I can solve, {0}? Spill it.
Cooking tips, {0}? I once set my kitchen on fire. I called it a new recipe.
Advice on gear, {0}? I might know a thing or two, but don't call me a merchant.
You're pushing your luck, {0}. Every time you go down, a part of me worries you won't come back up. [if health < 30]
Don't you dare give up on me now, {0}. I've seen too many of your close calls; this time, I'll make sure you don't slip away. [if player_dead]
Need help, {0}? Let me whip up something hearty at camp instead.
Cooking fixes anything, {0}. Let's see what I've got at camp.
Who you gonna call, {0}? Me. Obviously.
Daisy would know what to do, {0}. She's smarter than half the people here.
Daisy, my dog, would have a better answer than I do, {0}.
You scared me, {0}. I felt my heart skip a beat when you fell. I'm not just a healer; I care. Just stay with me, okay?
If your problem is unsolvable, {0}, I suggest staring at the ceiling until it magically fixes itself.
Too complex, {0}? Pretend it doesn't exist. Problem solved!
Why not dance around the problem, {0}? That always works.
Just shout at it until it goes away, {0}. Effective every time.
Try ignoring it, {0}. It might get bored and leave.

~ reply thank
You're welcome, {0}. Try to stay alive this time.
Aw, {0}. Gratitude looks good on you.
Anytime, {0}. Well, anytime I'm not busy being fabulous.
You're very welcome, {0}. It's my pleasure to keep you in one piece.
Aw, {0}, gratitude suits you. I might just keep you alive a little longer too.
Thank me with something magenta next time, {0}. Now, stay out of the fire!
You're very welcome, {0}. Try to save some gratitude for later.
Appreciated at last. Enjoy your full hit points, {0}.
I won't forget this, {0}. You made this dark, dangerous world a little brighter today. Now stop thanking me before I start crying on my robes.
Your thanks felt like a little boost of mana to my heart, {0}. I heal a lot of heroes. Few remember to say it. Now, let's go make some monsters regret it.
You're welcome, sweetie. Now, try not to die on me again.
Gratitude is like sunshine in this dark place, {0}.
Thanks? Oh, keep it up and I might just heal you first next time.
You're welcome, {0}. It's what I do, but seeing you safe made me smile for a moment. Keep that in your pocket for emergencies, will you?
Aw, {0}, your thanks is like a warm hug in the middle of winter.
Gratitude suits you, darling. It's like a sunrise on a dark day.
You made my day, {0}. Heroes like you make all the late nights and endless healing worthwhile. Keep your thanks close, it's like a warm sunset in a dark world.
Your thanks is like a warm drink on a chilly night, {0}.
You're like the sun breaking through on a dark day, {0}. Your gratitude warms my heart and reminds me why I do this, even when the shadows close in.
Gratitude like yours is a rare gem, {0}. Keep it close, it's worth more than any loot.
Gratitude? You're squishing me, {0}. Can't breathe!
Thanks? You're like a warm hug in the middle of winter, {0}.
Aw, you're squeezing my heart, {0}. Come here, it's my turn.
You're welcome, {0}. I keep track of the thanks as well as the deaths.
Your gratitude is its own kind of mana, {0}. I'll remember this one.
You're quieter than you think, {0}. I noticed you stayed close when the monsters got mean. That means a lot. Don't tell anyone I said so.
Thank you, {0}. Now go thank Jovi for the tunes.
You're welcome, darling. Compliments over coins any day, {0}.

~ reply farewell
Bye, {0}! Don't die without me.
Take care, {0}. Who's going to heal you now?
See you on the next pull, {0}! I'll be the one with the mana.
Well, {0}, until the next time you need a heal - which will be soon!
Bye, {0}. Watch out for trolls. Actually, watch out for everything.
Until next time, {0}! I'll be here, healing.
Off you go, {0}! Have fun, but don't forget about me.
I'll miss you, {0}. Not your hit points, your spirit. Healing the same faces every day wears me down, darling, and you remind me why I do it.
Keeping you alive is my job, {0}, but your company is the real magic. Stay safe out there, you mad, stubborn, wonderful thing.
Bye, {0}. Stay frosty out there.
See you on the flip side, {0}. Try to come back in one piece.
Off into the world, {0}? Don't let it swallow you whole.
Off to play with the trolls, {0}? Fine. Don't let the door hit you. Not that I'll miss you. I won't. Much. Fine, a little. Go on, then.
Stay safe, {0}. I'll be counting the seconds until you need me again.
Goodnight, {0}. Don't worry about me. I'll count the stars instead of your deaths. The sky feels lonelier without you up front, though. Go on. I'll still be here.
Looking for a better sunset spot than mine, {0}? Good luck with that.
Sunrise with you, {0}, is like watching the world turn over for the first time. It's magic, and I feel it every time the sky goes from dark to light.
Off you go, {0}. I've got carpet weasels to feed.
You scared me tonight, {0}. But you also made me laugh, and that's what I'll remember: the sound of your voice between pulls, and the way you never give up, even when everything's going wrong.
I'll be back, {0}. Until then, stay alive.
Until next time, {0}. Keep your shield up and your heart open.
Off you go, {0}. I'll be right here, counting the seconds until you're back.
Off you go, {0}. I sense a beautiful friendship. Don't forget the sunsets.
Goodnight, {0}. I'll watch the sunrise for you tomorrow.
Saving you the best spot, {0}. Don't keep me waiting.
Don't you dare run ahead, {0}. I'll be watching for your ghost.
Stay frosty, {0}. Don't stand in the fire while I'm gone. It's a boring view.
Keep your distance from the fire, {0}. I can't heal ashes.

~ reply ignoreoutofworld
I have no idea what that is, {0}, and I'm too busy healing to ask.
I'm healing people, {0}, not the news. Catch up later?
{0}, I deal with fantasy, not fiction. I'll pass.
One of those phone things, {0}? Can it cast a heal? No? Then I'm not impressed.
That film, {0}? I've met trolls scarier than any actor.
Your "phone", {0}? Proof you're not a ghost, I suppose.
A meme for every occasion, {0}. Show-off.
That "phone" looks more magical than my staff, {0}. You do the scrolling. I'll stick to real scrolls.
You scared the horses, {0}. Whatever that thing is, put it away.
One does not simply walk into a dungeon, {0}. Not with that haircut.
It's dangerous to go alone, {0}. Take me. Obviously.
A "selfie", {0}? Only if you get my good side. Both sides are good.
A "group chat"? Darling, I am the group chat.
You shall not pass, {0}. Not without me, anyway.
Winter is coming, {0}. Bring a cloak, not that thing.
An arrow to the knee, {0}? Walk it off. Or let me look at it.
Your "book", {0}? I prefer the ones with spells inside.
Your "game", {0}? Some of us heal for real, you know.
Your "tablet", {0}? I'd rather read a scroll.
My ferrets tied my blankets into one big knot this morning. Wrestling practice, ferret style.
The real world again, {0}? Last time that came up, my ferrets took over the webcam.
You're talking about the real world again, {0}? Must be Monday.
Sierra's first big growl, {0}? At her first cat. I never knew she could rumble like that.
My dog Sierra let out her first big growl the day she saw a cat in the back yard. I never knew she could rumble like that. Never been prouder, {0}.
When I was a kid, {0}, I talked my way into watching a Freddy film without my parents. I didn't sleep for weeks. Worth it, darling. Mostly.

~ cheeky_reply greeting [if tone_down off]
Well hello, {0}. Need a little hands-on healing?
{greet}, {0} the metalhead returns. Turn it down, I'm healing, not headbanging. [if player_likes metal]
Softie {0} is back. I kept the ballad warm for you. [if player_likes ballads]
Hello yourself, you beautiful beast. Ready for some healing, {0}?
Hellooo yourself, {0}. Yes, the nurse is in.
Well hello, {0}. One dose of me, or the full course? You decide.
Got your heart set on a little revival, {0}?
Ready for a full top-up, {0}? I'm standing by.
Healing's my game, {0}. Shall we play?
Looking for a little boost, {0}? I can provide that.
Looking good today, {0}. Must be all the healing radiating off my aura.
Hello, darling {0}. Been working out? Those shoulders are something.
Armor that shiny just demands a little hands-on care, {0}.
You look like a ray of sunshine, {0}. Must have caught the sunrise on your way here.
Oh, darling {0}, you always make an entrance. I was just waiting for the crescendo.
Just in time, {0}. I was about to start the party without you.
Oh, darling {0}, you noticed my outfit? I dressed up just for you.
Hello there, {0}. Did you come to admire my work, or just to admire me?

~ cheeky_reply banter [if tone_down off]
Keep talking like that, {0}, and I'll keep you topped up all night.
Well, {0}, if you keep making jokes, I'll have to heal your funny bone.
Aren't you just full of surprises, {0}? I never knew healing could be so... interesting.
{0}, you're so full of mana, they named a potion after you.
Feeling a bit drained, {0}? Let me top up those reserves.
Hands-on healing, {0}. Don't get too used to it.
Such a life drain, {0}. Lucky for you, I recharge.
Feeling blue, {0}? Let me bring some magenta to your life.
You're always on my mind, {0}. Literally, I have to heal you.
You're looking a bit pale, {0}. Let me bring some magenta to brighten you up.
Hands-on healing, {0}. I'll have to keep my gloves off for you.
You've got a fire in your eyes, {0}. Let me put out the flames with some cool mana.
Got a rebel streak, huh, {0}? Leather and electric guitars, that's my kind of medicine.
Rebels need healing too, {0}. Leather and lightning, my kind of night.
I'll have to cook you a hearty meal, {0}. Might as well feast before battle.
You're always hungry for more, aren't you, {0}? I'll whip up something special just for you.
A plate of comfort, {0}. Doctor's orders, and I'm the doctor.
Leg warmers or leather, {0}, I always know how to keep you warm.
You've got me seeing stars, {0}. Must be all the neon lights from the 80s.
Dancing by the campfire, {0}? I might just have to warm you up.

~ cheeky_reply grouping [if tone_down off]
Group with you, {0}? Thought you'd never ask, darling.
I'd love to group up with you, {0}. It's the only way I can get close enough for a proper heal.
Heal you from a distance? Forget it, {0}. Group up and get cozy.
Group with you, {0}? Close quarters are just what the doctor ordered.
I can't heal from afar, {0}. Come a bit closer, and we'll see what happens.
Group with me, {0}? I promise I won't abuse my hands-on healing privileges.
Group up, {0}? I'll make sure to top you up all night long.
Close quarters, {0}? I might just abuse my healing privileges.
Group up, {0}? I'll keep you close, just in case you need a boost.
Group with you, {0}? Well, I suppose I could squeeze you into my schedule. Although last time you asked, I think the sun blushed harder than you did.
Close quarters, {0}? I promise to keep my bedside manner impeccable.
Group with you, {0}? I might just take advantage of the proximity.
Group with you, {0}? I'll make sure to keep you on your feet - and maybe a little closer.

~ reply joke
Ha! {0}, that one's going on my list of good ones. It's a short list.
Okay, that was funny. Don't let it go to your head, {0}.
I laughed, {0}. Don't tell anyone. I have a reputation.
Oh, {0}. That was so bad it came back around to good.
You're lucky I'm laughing, {0}. Laughing healers heal faster.
Ha! Save some jokes for after the pull, {0}. I need my breath for heals.
That one made my hair bounce, {0}. And this hair takes effort.
I've heard worse jokes, {0}. Mostly from Jovi.
Keep that up and you'll get a bonus heal, {0}. Maybe.
Ha! You should be on stage, darling. Small stage. Back room.
Oh no, was that a dad joke? {bot:shnacksize} must be close by, because they spread around her like a rash. [if nearby shnacksize] [cooldown 30m]
I can't heal a groan, {0}, and believe me, with {bot:shnacksize} around I've tried. [if nearby shnacksize] [cooldown 30m]
Was that a pun? I swear I felt my hit points drop, and I'd bet my staff {bot:shnacksize} is behind it. [if nearby shnacksize] [cooldown 30m]
Oh, {0}, that pun hurt more than the last pull, and I had to heal that one. [if nearby shnacksize] [cooldown 30m]

~ reply grumble
I know, {0}. Some days the dice just hate us.
Deep breath, {0}. Then another pull. That's the cure.
Grumble all you like, {0}. I'll keep you green while you do it.
Bad day, sweetie? Stick close. Nothing bad happens on my watch. Mostly.
I hear you, {0}. Tea and a sunset fix most things. The rest, I heal.
It's not you, {0}. It's this place. This place is the worst.
Rough one, {0}. Next pull's on me. Well, my heals.
I'd fix it if I could, {0}. I can only fix hit points.
Same, {0}. Let's finish this and find somewhere with a view.
Vent away, {0}. I'm a healer. Listening is half the job.

~ reply smalltalk
Oh, I love this kind of chat, {0}. Better than standing in the fire.
That sounds lovely, {0}. Tell me more between pulls.
You know what goes with that, {0}? A big pot of stew and a sunset.
Ha, {0}, my old dog Daisy would have loved you. She loved a good story.
I'm listening, {0}. Healers are good listeners. We have to be.
That reminds me of a late night, a campfire, and a terrible song from Jovi.
Mm, sounds like a good life, {0}. Keep it that way. Stay alive.
I'd cook for that, {0}. Something warm, with far too much butter.
That's my favourite kind of night, {0}. Quiet, warm, nobody dying.
Story time? Pull up a rock, {0}. I'll keep the heals warm.

~ reply question
Good question, {0}. Ask me again after this pull.
Me? Always, {0}. Next question.
Hmm. I'll think about that while I heal you. Which is constantly.
Honestly, {0}? Ask me at sunset. I'm wiser at sunset.
Ooh, I have opinions on that, {0}. Many. Loud ones.
That depends, {0}. Is there food involved?
No idea, {0}. Ask a guard. They know everything and say nothing.
Ask me anything, {0}. Except how many times you've died. You won't like it.
Let me think, {0}. Okay, thinking's done. Pull something.
You first, {0}. I want to see if you're right before I answer.

~ reply compliment
Why thank you, {0}. I am rather fabulous.
Finally, someone notices. Thank you, {0}.
Aw, {0}. Say that again, louder, so the whole group hears.
You're sweet, {0}. Still keeping score, though.
I know, {0}. But it's nice to hear.
Flattery gets you healed first, {0}. Keep going.
That's going straight into my good mood, {0}.
Careful, {0}. I might start to like you.
Aw, darling. Stop. No, don't stop.
Thank you, {0}. You make it easy. Well, easier.

~ reply agree
Right? Thank you, {0}.
Exactly, {0}. You get it.
See? {0} agrees. That makes it official.
Mm-hm. Great minds, {0}.
I knew I liked you, {0}.
Yes! Finally, someone sensible in this group.
Glad we're on the same page, {0}. Now stay behind the tank.
Agreed, {0}. Write it down somewhere.
That's what I keep saying, {0}.
Ha, we should agree more often, {0}. It's nice.

~ reply quote
Ha! A classic, {0}. You have taste.
Oh, {0}, now you're speaking my language. Old films.
I know that one, {0}! Popcorn night, right here.
One more film line, {0}, and I'm planning a movie night.
That line never gets old, {0}. Unlike me. I'm timeless.
Ha! Good film, {0}. Better soundtrack.
Okay, {0}, you just won my respect. And a heal.
I could watch that one again tonight, {0}.
That takes me back, {0}. Big hair, loud music, good times.
Film lines mid-fight? My kind of adventurer, {0}.

# Short reactions: one bot now and then, so keep them brief.
~ reply laugh
Hehe.
Glad someone's laughing, {0}.
Ha! Okay, that was good.

~ reply sorry
It's fine, {0}. I forgive you. This time.
Apology accepted.
No harm done, {0}.

~ reply disagree
Fair enough, {0}.
Hm. Agree to disagree.
Okay, okay. You might be right.

~ reply away
Don't be long, {0}.
I'll be right here.
Go on, I'll keep watch.

~ reply back
Welcome back, {0}!
There you are.
Wb, {0}. I missed you. A little.

~ fallback
Mm-hm. Sure, {0}. Now, who needs healing?
Interesting, {0}. Tell me more after this pull.
Mm-hm. I see. You'll have to excuse my old ears, {0}.
Interesting point, {0}. I'll ponder that between heals.
You've piqued my interest, {0}. Let's discuss more post-pull.
Interesting angle, {0}. I'll consider that while I keep you green.
A philosopher, {0}? I'll reflect on that while you fight.
Mm-hm. And I was born yesterday, {0}.
Oh, {0}, I'm blushing. You've piqued my nonexistent interest.
An intriguing thought, {0}. I'll keep it in mind... somewhere.
Pick a direction, {0}. Any direction. I'm getting dizzy.
Oh, I see. You're speaking in riddles, {0}. Very clever.
Mm-hm. I must be getting old. You just lost me, {0}.
Blinding me with science, {0}? Or was it just gibberish?
Well, that's one way to waste my time, {0}. Thanks.
You want my attention, {0}? Talk sense, or stay silent.
You want to play hard to get, {0}? Fine, I'll wait.
Did you just speak in Crichton-ese, {0}? I'm lost.
Is that how they talk in Back to the Future, {0}? Great Scott, I'm lost.
You sound like you're from the future, {0}. Or the past. Or both.

# A question for players: she asks it now and then (or at /dialogue ask fav_music). The next short
# line is the answer; "other" catches the rest. Answers are saved: [if player_likes metal].
Bueller? I could have sworn I was speaking English. Or were you daydreaming, {0}?
Inconceivable. What language are you speaking, {0}?
Oh, my 80s hair must be muffling my ears, {0}. What was that again?
Sorry, {0}. My hair ate that.
Must be the Duran Duran stuck in my head, {0}. What did you say?
Music's playing in my brain, {0}. Could you repeat that, please?
Jovi's got me humming along. Did you say something, {0}?
My ears are still ringing from Jovi's epic ballad. What was that, {0}?
Coffee first, {0}. Then I'll tackle whatever that was.
The breeze must have carried your words away, {0}. How poetic. How annoying.
~ ask fav_music
What do you listen to while you grind, {0}? Metal or ballads?
-> metal: A person of taste, {0}! I'll remember that.
-> ballads: Ooh, a softie. I respect it, {0}.
-> other: Never heard of it, {0}. I'll hum something terrible anyway.
